{"slug":"findings","number":"9","title":"Findings and the report","file":"spec/rules/09-findings.md","sections":[{"id":"9.1","number":"9.1","title":"The report"},{"id":"9.2","number":"9.2","title":"Findings"},{"id":"9.3","number":"9.3","title":"Measured conditions"},{"id":"9.4","number":"9.4","title":"Elements and location"},{"id":"9.5","number":"9.5","title":"Wording"},{"id":"9.6","number":"9.6","title":"Display"},{"id":"9.7","number":"9.7","title":"Order"},{"id":"9.8","number":"9.8","title":"Serialization"},{"id":"9.9","number":"9.9","title":"The notice"}],"blocks":[{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.1","number":"9.1","c":["The report"]},{"t":"p","c":["An evaluation returns one ",{"t":"strong","c":["report"]},":"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Present"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"floorspecRules"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"0.1\""}],["always"],["the draft the report follows"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"notice"}],["string"],["always"],["the notice of ",{"t":"a","href":"#9.9","c":["9.9"]}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"units"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"imperial\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"metric\""}],["when step 1 of ",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/evaluation#1.3","c":["1.3"]}," passed"],["how values are displayed (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.6","c":["9.6"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"profile"}],["string"],["when step 2 passed"],["the profile's ",{"t":"code","v":"name"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"hash"}],["string"],["when step 3 passed"],["the document's content hash (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/serialization#9.3","c":["9.3"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"diagnostics"}],["array of diagnostics (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/diagnostics","c":["chapter 11"]},")"],["always"],["what is wrong with the request, its profile or its packs"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"evaluated"}],["array"],["always"],["every rule that was evaluated"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"notEvaluated"}],["array"],["always"],["every rule of a usable pack that was not, and why"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"coverage"}],["array"],["always"],["the coverage entries that apply"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"findings"}],["array of findings (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.2","c":["9.2"]},")"],["always"],["the findings"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["Each entry of ",{"t":"code","v":"evaluated"}," is ",{"t":"code","v":"{ \"pack\", \"version\", \"rule\", \"citation\", \"subjects\", \"exempt\", \"findings\" }"},": the pack's name and version, the rule's ID and citation, and how many subjects the rule had (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/rules#3.4","c":["3.4"]},"), how many of them were exempt (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/rules#3.7","c":["3.7"]},") and how many findings it gave (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/rules#3.6","c":["3.6"]},")."]},{"t":"p","c":["Each entry of ",{"t":"code","v":"notEvaluated"}," is ",{"t":"code","v":"{ \"pack\", \"version\", \"rule\", \"reason\" }"},", where ",{"t":"code","v":"reason"}," is ",{"t":"code","v":"\"profile\""}," when the profile does not select the rule's pack (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/profiles#10.4","c":["10.4"]},"), ",{"t":"code","v":"\"invalid\""}," for ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-RULES-007"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"deferred\""}," for ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-RULES-008"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"edition\""}," when the rule's edition is not in force (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/profiles#10.3","c":["10.3"]},"), ",{"t":"code","v":"\"withdrawn\""}," when an amendment withdraws it (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/profiles#10.5","c":["10.5"]},"), and ",{"t":"code","v":"\"extension\""}," for ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-RULES-009"},". A rule of a pack that is not usable (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/evaluation#1.3","c":["1.3"]},") is in neither list: its pack could not be read."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"coverage"}," holds the coverage entries (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/packs#2.4","c":["2.4"]},") of every usable pack the profile selects whose ",{"t":"code","v":"code"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"edition"}," are in force (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/profiles#10.2","c":["10.2"]},"), each with the member ",{"t":"code","v":"pack"},", its pack's name, added."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.1.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST return a report with exactly the members of this section, and MUST list every rule of every usable pack in exactly one of ",{"t":"code","v":"evaluated"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"notEvaluated"},", with the counts and the reason this section gives."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.1.2","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST list in ",{"t":"code","v":"coverage"}," exactly the coverage entries this section gives."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["A report says what was checked and what was found. It never lists what \"passed\": a rule with no finding is an entry of ",{"t":"code","v":"evaluated"}," whose ",{"t":"code","v":"findings"}," is 0, and a subject with no finding is not named at all."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.2","number":"9.2","c":["Findings"]},{"t":"p","c":["A ",{"t":"strong","c":["finding"]}," says that one subject may not meet one rule:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"pack"}],["string"],["the pack's name"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"version"}],["string"],["the pack's version"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"rule"}],["string"],["the rule's ID"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"title"}],["string"],["the rule's ",{"t":"code","v":"title"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"citation"}],["citation"],["the rule's citation, as the pack gives it: code, edition, section and link"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"severity"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"mayNotMeet\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"check\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"note\""}],["the rule's severity (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/rules#3.11","c":["3.11"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"subject"}],["target (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]},")"],["the subject"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"candidates"}],["array of targets"],["present when the rule selects (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/rules#3.5","c":["3.5"]},"): the subject's candidates, in order (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"measures"}],["array of measured conditions (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.3","c":["9.3"]},")"],["what was measured"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"elements"}],["array of IDs, sorted"],["what the finding is about (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.4","c":["9.4"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"location"}],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"level\": ID, \"shapes\": [shape, …] }"}],["where to draw it (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.4","c":["9.4"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"message"}],["string"],["the finding in words (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.5","c":["9.5"]},")"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.2.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST give every finding exactly the members of this section."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.3","number":"9.3","c":["Measured conditions"]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"measures"}," lists, for each target the requirement was evaluated on — the subject, or each candidate in order — each condition of the requirement in the order it is written (depth first, left to right through ",{"t":"code","v":"all"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"any"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"not"},"), every one of them, whether or not it decided the outcome:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"target"}],["target (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]},")"],["what was measured"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"measure"}],["string"],["the measure's name"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"args"}],["object"],["the condition's ",{"t":"code","v":"args"},", when it has them"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"type"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"value"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"display"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}],[],["the measure result (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.7","c":["4.7"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"op"}],["string"],["the condition's ",{"t":"code","v":"op"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"threshold"}],[],["the condition's ",{"t":"code","v":"value"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"thresholdDisplay"}],["string"],["the threshold as a person reads it (",{"t":"a","href":"#9.6","c":["9.6"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"holds"}],["boolean"],["whether the condition holds (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/rules#3.8","c":["3.8"]},")"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["A finding for a subject with no candidate, of a rule that needs any, has no measured condition: the finding's message and its empty ",{"t":"code","v":"candidates"}," say what is missing."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.3.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST list the measured conditions of a finding exactly as this section defines them."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.4","number":"9.4","c":["Elements and location"]},{"t":"p","c":["A finding's ",{"t":"code","v":"elements"}," are the subject's ID, each candidate's ID (an envelope's owner's), and every ID in the ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}," of its measured conditions, each once, sorted."]},{"t":"p","c":["Its ",{"t":"code","v":"location"}," is where a plan draws it: ",{"t":"code","v":"level"}," is the subject's level (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]},"), and ",{"t":"code","v":"shapes"}," lists, in this order and each once, the ",{"t":"strong","c":["shape"]}," of the subject, of each candidate in order, and of each ID of ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}," that has a shape, in ID order:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null],"head":[["Of"],["Shape"]],"rows":[[["a room"],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"kind\": \"polygon\", \"outer\": ring, \"holes\": [ring, …] }"},": its room polygon (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/rooms#6.2","c":["6.2"]},")"]],[["an opening"],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"kind\": \"segment\", \"points\": [start, end] }"},": its derived start and end points (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/openings#7.4","c":["7.4"]},")"]],[["an extension element"],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"kind\": \"polygon\", \"outer\": ring, \"holes\": [] }"},": its fallback's footprint (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/extensions#12.6","c":["12.6"]},")"]],[["a clearance envelope"],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"kind\": \"polygon\", \"outer\": ring, \"holes\": [] }"},": its footprint (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/hosting#13.5","c":["13.5"]},")"]],[["a wall"],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"kind\": \"polygon\", \"outer\": ring, \"holes\": [] }"},": its outline (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/walls#5.7","c":["5.7"]},"), starting at its least vertex"]],[["a stair"],[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"kind\": \"polygon\", \"outer\": ring, \"holes\": [] }"},": its box in plan (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/stairs#17.4","c":["17.4"]},") — ",{"t":"code","v":"[x₀, y₀]"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"[x₁, y₀]"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"[x₁, y₁]"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"[x₀, y₁]"}]],[["a level, a circuit"],["none"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["Every ring is as Core derives it: integer points, least vertex first, counter-clockwise for an outer ring and clockwise for a hole. So a finding about a panel's working space draws the panel, the space and whatever obstructs it, and one about a bedroom draws the room."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.4.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST give every finding the elements and the location this section defines."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.5","number":"9.5","c":["Wording"]},{"t":"p","c":["A finding's ",{"t":"code","v":"message"}," is written from a template, so that every finding of every evaluator reads the same and none says more than the rule can:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null],"head":[[{"t":"code","v":"severity"}],[{"t":"code","v":"message"}]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"\"mayNotMeet\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"<subject> may not meet <code> <edition> <section> (<title>)."}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"\"check\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"<subject> may not meet <code> <edition> <section> (<title>). Check it with a professional or the authority having jurisdiction."}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"\"note\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"<subject> may not meet <code> <edition> <section> (<title>). This is for information."}]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"<subject>"}," is the subject's ID; ",{"t":"code","v":"<code>"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"<edition>"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"<section>"}," are the rule's citation's; and ",{"t":"code","v":"<title>"}," is the rule's title. So a message names the edition it was checked against, every time: ",{"t":"code","v":"R2 may not meet IRC 2024 R310.1 (Escape opening in every sleeping room)."}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.5.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST write every finding's message exactly as this table gives it."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.5.2","level":"MUST NOT","c":["A report MUST NOT contain a match of the assurance pattern (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/packs#2.5","c":["2.5"]},") anywhere outside the IDs it copies from the document: no finding, message, display or entry says that a design complies with, meets or passes a code."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.6","number":"9.6","c":["Display"]},{"t":"p","c":["A measure result's ",{"t":"code","v":"display"},", and a measured condition's ",{"t":"code","v":"thresholdDisplay"},", give a value as a person reads it, in the request's ",{"t":"code","v":"units"},". Each is rounded once, with ",{"t":"code","v":"round()"},", from the exact value:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[["Type"],[{"t":"code","v":"\"imperial\""}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"metric\""}]],"rows":[[["length ",{"t":"code","v":"v"}],[{"t":"code","v":"n = round(v / 2032)"}," sixteenths of an inch, written ",{"t":"code","v":"F' I\""},", or ",{"t":"code","v":"F' I a/b\""}," with the fraction ",{"t":"code","v":"a/b"}," of an inch in lowest terms, where ",{"t":"code","v":"F"}," is the whole feet of `"],["n"]],[["area ",{"t":"code","v":"A"}],[{"t":"code","v":"n = round(100 · A / 152212340736)"}," hundredths of a square foot, written ",{"t":"code","v":"5.70 sq ft"}],[{"t":"code","v":"n = round(100 · A / 1638400000000)"}," hundredths of a square metre, written ",{"t":"code","v":"0.53 m²"}]],[["count, integer"],["the integer in decimal, followed by a space and its unit when it has one: ",{"t":"code","v":"20 A"}],["the same"]],[["boolean"],[{"t":"code","v":"yes"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"no"}],["the same"]],[["term"],["the term"],["the same"]],[["terms"],["the terms in order, separated by ",{"t":"code","v":", "},", or ",{"t":"code","v":"none"}," when there are none"],["the same"]],[["no value"],[{"t":"code","v":"not stated"}],["the same"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["So 390,144 base units display as ",{"t":"code","v":"1' 0\""},", 1,148,080 as ",{"t":"code","v":"2' 11 5/16\""},", and 152,212,340,736 square base units as ",{"t":"code","v":"1.00 sq ft"},". A threshold displays as a value of the measure's type; a threshold of ",{"t":"code","v":"in"}," displays each of its values, separated by ",{"t":"code","v":", "},". An area threshold, an integer of square base units, displays as an area."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.6.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST write every ",{"t":"code","v":"display"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"thresholdDisplay"}," exactly as this section defines them."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.7","number":"9.7","c":["Order"]},{"t":"p","c":["Every array of a report is in a defined order, so that a report is one value:"]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"diagnostics"}," by ",{"t":"code","v":"code"},", then ",{"t":"code","v":"packIndex"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"pack"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"rule"},", a member that is absent sorting first;"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"evaluated"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"notEvaluated"}," by ",{"t":"code","v":"pack"},", then ",{"t":"code","v":"rule"},";"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"coverage"}," by ",{"t":"code","v":"pack"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"code"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"edition"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"section"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"status"},", then ",{"t":"code","v":"note"},", an absent note first;"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"findings"}," by ",{"t":"code","v":"pack"},", then ",{"t":"code","v":"rule"},", then the subject (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]},");"]}],[{"t":"p","c":["every array of IDs, and ",{"t":"code","v":"candidates"},", as ",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]}," orders targets; ",{"t":"code","v":"measures"}," as ",{"t":"a","href":"#9.3","c":["9.3"]}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"shapes"}," as ",{"t":"a","href":"#9.4","c":["9.4"]}," list them."]}]]},{"t":"p","c":["Strings are compared as sequences of UTF-16 code units, as Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/serialization#9.2","c":["9.2"]}," compares member names."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.7.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST order every array of a report as this section defines."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.8","number":"9.8","c":["Serialization"]},{"t":"p","c":["A report is written as Floorspec Core writes a canonical document (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/serialization#9.2","c":["9.2"]},", step 2): object members sorted, two spaces of indentation per level, one line feed at the end. Two conformant evaluators given the same inputs produce the same bytes."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.8.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST write a report exactly as Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/serialization#9.2","c":["9.2"]},", step 2, writes a value."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"9.9","number":"9.9","c":["The notice"]},{"t":"p","c":["Every report carries this ",{"t":"strong","c":["notice"]},", exactly:"]},{"t":"quote","c":[{"t":"p","c":["Floorspec findings are advisory. They are not a plan review, and the authority having jurisdiction decides."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.9.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST give the notice, exactly as this section gives it, as the report's ",{"t":"code","v":"notice"},", in every report it returns."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-9.9.2","level":"SHOULD","c":["Software that shows findings to a person SHOULD show the notice wherever it shows a finding, with the coverage of the packs evaluated, and SHOULD NOT shorten or reword a finding's message."]}]}]}
